---
import CenteredPage from "../../layouts/CenteredPage.astro";
import SidePanel from "../../components/SidePanel.astro";

const title = "Tic Tac Tesseract";
const description = "Play Tic Tac Toe in a few more dimensions than usual. Same rules, more positions."
const version = 2.1;
---

<CenteredPage
        title={ title }
        description={ description }
        opts={{ background: true, buttons: true }}
>
    <div class="game">
        <div class="header">
            <div class="title">
                <h1 class="heading">{ title }</h1>
                <div class="version font-dotmatrix">v{ version }</div>
            </div>

            <p class="subtext">{ description }</p>
        </div>

        <div class="board">
            <div class="strip above">
                <div class="button font-dotmatrix">
                    <a onclick="togglePanel('guidePanel');" id="guideToggle">playing guide</a>
                </div>

                <div class="status">
                    <span class="player">player X</span>'s turn
                </div>
            </div>

            <div class="playfield-wrapper">
                <table id="playField"></table>

                <button type="button" id="resetBoard" class="reset-icon" aria-label="Reset board" title="Reset board" onclick="cleanBoard();">
                    <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
                        <polyline points="23 4 23 10 17 10"></polyline>
                        <polyline points="1 20 1 14 7 14"></polyline>
                        <path d="M20.49 15a9 9 0 0 1-14.85 3.36L1 14M23 10l-4.64-4.36A9 9 0 0 0 3.51 9"></path>
                    </svg>
                </button>
            </div>

            <div class="strip below">
                <div class="credit">
                    by <a href="https://linktr.ee/phantomeye" target="_blank">PhantomEye</a>
                    & <a href="https://linktr.ee/serialsniper" target="_blank">SerialSniper</a>
                </div>

                <div class="button font-dotmatrix">
                    <a onclick="toggleHardMode();" id="hardModeToggle">disable highlights</a>
                    <div class="square highlight"></div>
                    <div class="square highlightSecondary"></div>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>

    <SidePanel id="guidePanel" title="How to play" subtitle="(and why this is 4D)">
            <div class="guide-prose">
                <p>
                    Tic Tac Tesseract is a play on the classic game Tic Tac Toe. Like the original, it's played by two participants who take turns placing a piece in an empty cell, trying to get 4 of their pieces in a straight line, while blocking the other player from doing the same.
                </p>
                <p>
                    Instead of a 3x3 board, we play on a 4x4 board, since a 3x3 would make it too easy to force a win. Unlike normal Tic Tac Toe, this version is played in 4 dimensions — a 4x4x4x4 board, for 256 cells in total. Trying to visualize this can be tough, so it's best not to try to wrap your head around the geometry, and just get used to the rules of the game instead.
                </p>
                <p>
                    For simplicity, let's start with a 3D board. You can probably imagine how a 3D game would work: 4 of the same piece stacked directly above each other would win. Here's an example:
                </p>

                <figure class="tutorial-figure stack">
                    <img src="/pages/tic-tac-tesseract/guide/tutorial_3d_3dview_1.png" alt="3D example">
                    <figcaption>A straight line that goes directly up through a 3D board</figcaption>
                </figure>

                <p>
                    You can see 4 crosses positioned directly below each other, one per level — a win for player X. We can also represent this as four 4x4 fields next to each other, like below. Think of them as floors of a building: each field is a floor of our 4x4 board. If every floor has your piece in the same spot, you win.
                </p>

                <figure class="tutorial-figure">
                    <img src="/pages/tic-tac-tesseract/guide/tutorial_3d_1.png" alt="Floors example">
                    <figcaption>The same board represented as floors</figcaption>
                </figure>

                <p>
                    If you've played Tic Tac Toe before, you know you can also make diagonal lines to win. Here's an example:
                </p>

                <figure class="tutorial-figure stack">
                    <img src="/pages/tic-tac-tesseract/guide/tutorial_3d_3dview_2.png" alt="Diagonal 3D example">
                    <figcaption>A straight line that goes diagonally up through a 3D board</figcaption>
                </figure>

                <figure class="tutorial-figure">
                    <img src="/pages/tic-tac-tesseract/guide/tutorial_3d_2.png" alt="Diagonal floors example">
                    <figcaption>The same board represented as floors</figcaption>
                </figure>

                <p>
                    Here's another example, where player O blocked player X from winning:
                </p>

                <figure class="tutorial-figure">
                    <img src="/pages/tic-tac-tesseract/guide/tutorial_3d_3.png" alt="Blocking example">
                    <figcaption>A line blocked by player O</figcaption>
                </figure>

                <p>
                    Now that we've expanded into another dimension and flattened it out, we can repeat this process to expand into the 4th dimension. Imagine the bottom row of the following board is what we already established, and all rows above it are floors stacked on top of that board:
                </p>

                <figure class="tutorial-figure">
                    <img src="/pages/tic-tac-tesseract/guide/tutorial_4d_1.png" alt="4D win example">
                    <figcaption>A line going diagonal in all directions</figcaption>
                </figure>

                <p>
                    Here's what that looks like stacked on top of each other — our 4D board.
                </p>

                <figure class="tutorial-figure">
                    <img src="/pages/tic-tac-tesseract/guide/tutorial_4d_3dview.png" alt="4D board as 4 stacked 3D boards">
                    <figcaption>A 4D board represented as 4 3D boards</figcaption>
                </figure>

                <p>
                    Here are some of the straight lines you could make on this board to win:
                </p>

                <figure class="tutorial-figure">
                    <img src="/pages/tic-tac-tesseract/guide/tutorial_4d_2.png" alt="Valid line examples">
                    <figcaption>Examples of valid lines</figcaption>
                </figure>

                <p>
                    To make the game easier to follow, the lines your hovered cell could be part of are highlighted like below. You can turn this off by clicking "disable highlights" below the board for an extra challenge — or add <code>?hard</code> to the end of the url.
                </p>

                <figure class="tutorial-figure">
                    <img src="/pages/tic-tac-tesseract/guide/tutorial_4d_3.png" alt="Highlight example">
                    <figcaption>Highlights of lines the hovered cell could form</figcaption>
                </figure>

                <p>
                    That's it! It's a confusing game at first, but it becomes much more intuitive as you get used to the rules. Here's an example of a real game where player X won:
                </p>

                <figure class="tutorial-figure">
                    <img src="/pages/tic-tac-tesseract/guide/tutorial_4d_4.png" alt="Real game example">
                    <figcaption>An example of a real game — player X won here</figcaption>
                </figure>

                <p class="final-line">Have fun playing!</p>
            </div>
    </SidePanel>
</CenteredPage>

<script>
    import svgX from '/pages/tic-tac-tesseract/game/cross.svg?raw';
    import svgO from '/pages/tic-tac-tesseract/game/circle.svg?raw';

    const urlParams = new URLSearchParams(window.location.search);
    let hardMode = urlParams.get("hard") != null;

    if ('serviceWorker' in navigator) {
        navigator.serviceWorker.register('service-worker.js');
    }

    let lastMove: Vec4 | null = null;

    // Generates the playing field
    for (let w = 0; w < 4; w++) {
        let row = $("<tr></tr>").appendTo("#playField").on("mouseleave",function() {
            removeClasses('highlights');
            highlightLastMove();
        });

        for (let z = 0; z < 4; z++) {
            let cell = $("<td></td>").appendTo(row);
            for (let y = 0; y < 4; y++) {
                let innerTableRow = $("<tr></tr>").appendTo(cell);
                for (let x = 0; x < 4; x++) {
                    $("<td><div class='none'></td>").appendTo(innerTableRow)
                        .attr("id", `${x}${y}${z}${w}`)
                        .on("mouseenter", function() {
                            // When hovering a cell, highlight the cell by passing the coordinates stored in the cell ID
                            removeClasses('highlights');
                            highlightLastMove();
                            highlightPossible($(this).attr("id") as CoordinateString);
                        });
                }
            }
        }
    }

    let secondaryTurn = false; // Storing whose turn it is
    let gameEnded = false;
    let turnDisplay = $(".status"); // Gets the text element above the playing field
    let resetIcon = $("#resetBoard"); // Shown centered over the board once a player wins

    // Make all cells clickable
    const playFieldElement = $("#playField");

    playFieldElement.on('click', function(event) {
        const clicked = $(event.target);

        if (gameEnded) return;

        // If the cell is empty, fills it with the current player's symbol
        let empty = Number.isInteger(parseInt(clicked.attr("id") ?? ' ')) && clicked.find("div").hasClass("none");
        if (empty) {
            secondaryTurn = !secondaryTurn // Flip whose turn it is
            clicked.find("div").removeClass("none");
            clicked.find("div").addClass(secondaryTurn ? "x" : "o"); // Place the symbol
            lastMove = Vec4.parse(clicked.attr("id"));

            highlightLastMove();
            if (!hardMode) highlightPossible($(this).attr("id") as CoordinateString);

            // Update the text above the playing field
            const symbol = secondaryTurn ? 'O' : 'X';
            const statusText = checkForWin(clicked.attr("id") ?? ' ')
                ? `<span class="player">player ${symbol}</span> won!`
                : (`<span class="player">player ${symbol}</span>\'s turn`);
            turnDisplay.html(statusText);

            renderPieces();
        }
    });

    type Coordinate = 0 | 1 | 2 | 3;
    type CoordinateString = `${Coordinate}${Coordinate}${Coordinate}${Coordinate}`;

    class Vec4 {
        constructor(
            public x: Coordinate,
            public y: Coordinate,
            public z: Coordinate,
            public w: Coordinate,
        ) {};

        // Parse from a string, eg. 0000
        static parse(str: any) {
            return new Vec4(str[0], str[1], str[2], str[3]);
        }

        // Get one of the values based on index
        get(i: number) {
            switch(i) {
                case 0: return this.x;
                case 1: return this.y;
                case 2: return this.z;
                case 3: return this.w;
                default: return null;
            }
        }

        toString(): CoordinateString {
            return `${this.x}${this.y}${this.z}${this.w}`;
        }

        toArray() {
            return [ this.x, this.y, this.z, this.w ];
        }

        clone() {
            return new Vec4(this.x, this.y, this.z, this.w);
        }

        static fromBase3(n: number) {
            let out = new Vec4(0, 0, 0, 0);

            out.x = n % 3 as Coordinate;
            n = Math.floor(n / 3);
            out.y = n % 3 as Coordinate;
            n = Math.floor(n / 3);
            out.z = n % 3 as Coordinate;
            n = Math.floor(n / 3);
            out.w = n % 3 as Coordinate;

            return out;
        }
    }

    // Remove certain classes from all cells
    function removeClasses(classes: 'lastMove' | 'pieces' | 'highlights') {
        for (let w = 0; w < 4; w++)
            for (let z = 0; z < 4; z++)
                for (let y = 0; y < 4; y++)
                    for (let x = 0; x < 4; x++) {
                        let cell = $(`#${x}${y}${z}${w} > div`);

                        switch (classes) {
                            case 'lastMove':
                                cell.removeClass("highlightLastMove");
                                break;
                            case 'pieces':
                                cell
                                    .removeClass("x")
                                    .removeClass("o")
                                    .removeClass("highlightLastMove")
                                    .removeClass("highlightWinning")
                                    .addClass("none");
                                break;
                            case 'highlights':
                                cell
                                    .removeClass("highlight")
                                    .removeClass("highlightGray")
                                    .removeClass("highlightSecondary");
                                break;
                        }
                    }
    }

    // Check if the last placed cell finishes a line, returns boolean
    function checkForWin(coordinates: string): boolean {
        let clicked = Vec4.parse(coordinates);
        for (let i = 0; i < Math.pow(3, 4); i++) {
            // Convert i to base-3
            let iterator = Vec4.fromBase3(i);

            // Ensure the line we're checking is valid
            if (!ensureAtLeastOneOne(iterator)) continue;

            // Checks whether the clicked cell is on the line
            if (!isInCombination(clicked, iterator)) continue;

            // Check the 4 cells within the line
            let countOnLine = 0;
            for (let j = 0; j < 4; j++) {
                let drawIterator = checkLine(iterator, clicked, j);
                let coordinateString: CoordinateString = drawIterator.toString();

                // Check if the cell contains the right symbol, if so, increment countOnLine
                let $div = $(`#${coordinateString}`).find("div");
                if ($div.hasClass(secondaryTurn ? "x" : "o") && coordinateString != coordinates) {
                    countOnLine++;
                }
            }

            // If the entire line is filled with the right symbol (clicked + 3 extra = 4), mark the game as won
            if (countOnLine == 3) {
                highlightWinningPieces(iterator, clicked);
                removeClasses('highlights');

                gameEnded = true;
                resetIcon.addClass("visible");
                playFieldElement.addClass("ended");
                return true;
            }
        }
        return false;
    }

    // Creates a Vec4 to check cells in a line
    function checkLine(iterator: Vec4, selected: Vec4, j: number) {
        return new Vec4(
            // = 0: it's static
            // = 1: it's equal to the incrementing j
            // = 2: it's equal to the inverse of j (3 - j)
            iterator.x == 0 ? selected.x : (iterator.x == 1 ? j : (3 - j)) as Coordinate,
            iterator.y == 0 ? selected.y : (iterator.y == 1 ? j : (3 - j)) as Coordinate,
            iterator.z == 0 ? selected.z : (iterator.z == 1 ? j : (3 - j)) as Coordinate,
            iterator.w == 0 ? selected.w : (iterator.w == 1 ? j : (3 - j)) as Coordinate,
        );
    }

    // Highlights the last move made
    function highlightLastMove() {
        if (lastMove != null) {
            removeClasses('lastMove')
            addClass(lastMove, "highlightLastMove");
        }
    }

    // Highlights the winning 4 cells
    function highlightWinningPieces(iterator: Vec4, selected: Vec4) {
        for (let j = 0; j < 4; j++) {
            let drawIterator = checkLine(iterator, selected, j);

            // Adds the winning highlight to the 4 cells of the line
            addClass(drawIterator, "highlightWinning");
        }
    }

    // Highlights all the possible combinations
    function highlightPossible(coordinates: CoordinateString) {
        // Don't highlight if the game has ended
        if (gameEnded) return;

        let selected = Vec4.parse(coordinates); // Get a vector of the selected cell

        if (hardMode) addClass(selected, "highlightGray");

        // Goes over all possible lines
        if (!hardMode) {
            for (let i = 0; i < Math.pow(3, 4); i++) {
                // Convert i to base-3
                let iterator = Vec4.fromBase3(i);

                // Ensure the line we're checking is valid
                if (!ensureAtLeastOneOne(iterator)) continue;

                // Checks whether the hovered cell is in the line
                if (!isInCombination(selected, iterator)) continue;

                // Highlight the 4 cells in the line
                for (let j = 0; j < 4; j++) {
                    let drawIterator = checkLine(iterator, selected, j);
                    addClass(drawIterator, "highlightSecondary");
                }
            }
            addClass(selected, "highlight");
        }
        // Add highlights to the cell that's being hovered
        removeClass(selected, "highlightSecondary");
    }

    // Adds a class to an element
    function addClass(coordinates: Vec4, cssClass: string) {
        if (coordinates != null) {
            $(`#${coordinates.toString()} > div`).addClass(cssClass);
        }
    }

    // Removes a class from an element
    function removeClass(coordinates: Vec4, cssClass: string) {
        $(`#${coordinates.toString()} > div`).removeClass(cssClass);
    }

    // Ensures that at least one value in the vector is 1
    function ensureAtLeastOneOne(vec: Vec4) {
        return vec.x == 1
            || vec.y == 1
            || vec.z == 1
            || vec.w == 1;
    }

    // Check if the selected cell is on a line
    function isInCombination(pos: Vec4, combination: Vec4) {
        // Creates a temporary copy of pos so it won't be overwritten
        let posTemp = pos.clone();

        // Inverts the value if the axis is reversed, indicated by a value of 2
        if (combination.x == 2) posTemp.x = 3 - posTemp.x as Coordinate;
        if (combination.y == 2) posTemp.y = 3 - posTemp.y as Coordinate;
        if (combination.z == 2) posTemp.z = 3 - posTemp.z as Coordinate;
        if (combination.w == 2) posTemp.w = 3 - posTemp.w as Coordinate;

        let num = -1;
        let posTempArray = posTemp.toArray();
        for (let i = 0; i < 4; i++) {
            // If the axis is static, skip it
            if (combination.get(i) == 0)
                continue;
            // Only set num if the combination axis isn't 0
            if (num == -1)
                num = posTempArray[i];
            // Stop checking if one of the axes doesn't match
            if (posTempArray[i] != num)
                return false;
        }
        return true;
    }

    // Resets the board to start a new game
    function cleanBoard() {
        removeClasses('highlights');
        removeClasses('pieces');
        lastMove = null;
        gameEnded = false;
        secondaryTurn = false;
        turnDisplay.html('<span class="player">player X</span>\'s turn');
        resetIcon.removeClass("visible");
        playFieldElement.removeClass("ended");
    }

    function renderPieces() {
        for (let w = 0; w < 4; w++)
            for (let z = 0; z < 4; z++)
                for (let y = 0; y < 4; y++)
                    for (let x = 0; x < 4; x++) {
                        let cell = $(`#${x}${y}${z}${w} > div`);

                        if (cell.hasClass('x')) {
                            cell.html(svgX);
                            continue;
                        }
                        if (cell.hasClass('o')) {
                            cell.html(svgO);
                            continue;
                        }

                        cell.remove("svg");
                    }
    }

    let hardModeToggle = $("#hardModeToggle");

    // Toggles whether move hints are shown
    function toggleHardMode() {
        hardMode = !hardMode;
        hardModeToggle.html(hardMode ? 'enable highlights' : 'disable highlights');

        if (hardMode) hardModeToggle.parent().find(".square").addClass("disabled");
        if (!hardMode) hardModeToggle.parent().find(".square").removeClass("disabled");
    }

    // Expose to the inline onclick handlers, which run outside this module's scope
    (window as any).cleanBoard = cleanBoard;
    (window as any).toggleHardMode = toggleHardMode;
</script>

<style is:global>
    :root {
        --highlight-grayscale: #929aa3;
        --highlight-hover:     #d4779a;
        --highlight-connected: #70b6c2;
        --highlight-win:       #53e164;
        --highlight-recent:    #dcc050;

        /* Combined colors */
        --highlight-recent-hover: #d3bcdc;
        --highlight-recent-connected: #a9d6a7;
    }

    [color-scheme='dark'] {
        --highlight-grayscale: #6e757c;
        --highlight-hover: #803f6d;
        --highlight-connected: #3a6271;
        --highlight-win: #2c8854;
        --highlight-recent: #6c4e14;

        /* Combined colors */
        --highlight-recent-hover: #856191;
        --highlight-recent-connected: #6b816d;
    }

    .game {
        display: flex;
        flex-direction: column;
        min-width: 0;

        padding: 0 2em;

        background-color: var(--col-background);
    }

    /* Panel chrome (open/close, scrolling, sticky/mobile-fullscreen) lives in SidePanel.astro now -
       this is just the guide's own prose styling for the content inside it */
    .guide-prose {
        & p {
            line-height: 1.5;
            margin: 0 0 1rem;
        }

        & code {
            background-color: var(--col-background-2);
            padding: 0.1rem 0.3rem;
        }
    }

    .tutorial-figure {
        margin: 0 0 1.25rem;
        text-align: center;

        & img {
            max-width: 100%;
            border: 1px solid var(--col-border-2);
        }

        & figcaption {
            margin-top: 0.4rem;
            font-size: 0.85rem;
            color: var(--col-text-2);
        }

        &.stack img {
            max-width: 10rem;
        }
    }

    .final-line {
        font-weight: bold;
        text-align: center;
    }

    .header {
        display: flex;
        flex-direction: column;
        gap: 0.5rem;

        max-width: 30rem;
        padding-bottom: 1rem;

        & > .title {
            display: flex;
            align-items: baseline;
            gap: 0.5rem;

            margin-bottom: -2.5rem;
        }

        & > .subtext {
            color: var(--col-text-2);
            margin-bottom: 4px;
        }
    }

    .strip {
        display: flex;
        flex-direction: row;
        justify-content: space-between;

        padding-block: 0.6rem;

        &.above {
            align-items: flex-end;
        }
    }

    .button {
        display: flex;
        flex-direction: row;
        gap: 0.4rem;
        align-items: center;

        border: 2px solid var(--col-border-2);
        padding: 0.2rem 0.4rem;

        cursor: pointer;
        user-select: none;

        & > a {
            color: inherit;
            text-decoration: none;
        }

        & > .square {
            width: 0.8rem;
            height: 0.8rem;
            border: 1px solid var(--col-border-2);

            &.disabled {
                background-color: var(--highlight-grayscale) !important;
            }
        }

        &:hover {
            opacity: 0.7;
        }
    }

    .status {
        color: var(--col-text-2);
        text-align: right;

        & > .player {
            font-weight: bold;
            color: var(--col-cmyk-magenta);
        }
    }

    .board {
        margin-inline: 3em;
    }

    .playfield-wrapper {
        position: relative;
        container-type: inline-size;
        width: min(534px, 90vw);
    }

    .reset-icon {
        all: unset;
        display: none;
        position: absolute;
        top: 50%;
        left: 50%;
        transform: translate(-50%, -50%);

        align-items: center;
        justify-content: center;
        box-sizing: border-box;
        width: 2.5rem;
        height: 2.5rem;

        background-color: var(--col-background);
        border: 2px solid var(--col-border-2);

        color: var(--col-text-2);
        cursor: pointer;

        svg {
            width: 1.5rem;
            height: 1.5rem;
        }

        &:hover {
            background-color: var(--col-background-2);
        }

        &.visible {
            display: flex;
        }
    }

    #playField {
        --cell-size: clamp(14px, calc(6.25cqw - 3.375px), 30px);

        border: solid 2px var(--col-border-1);
        border-spacing: 0;
        user-select: none;

        &.ended {
            pointer-events: none;
        }
    }

    #playField > tr > td {
        position: relative;
    }

    #playField > tr > td {
        background-color: var(--col-background-2);
    }

    /* Cell */
    #playField > tr > td > tr > td {
        cursor: pointer;
    }

    #playField > tr > td > tr > td > div {
        width: var(--cell-size);
        height: var(--cell-size);
        background-color: var(--col-background);

        background-position: 50% 50%;
        background-size: 70%;
        background-repeat: no-repeat;

        display: flex;
        align-items: center;
        justify-content: center;
        pointer-events: none;
    }

    .credit {
        opacity: 0.7;
        color: var(--col-cmyk-cyan);

        & > a {
            color: var(--col-text-2);
            text-decoration: none;
            font-weight: bold;
        }
    }

    /* Game icons */
    svg {
        width: 80%;
        height: 80%;
        --4dttt-icon-fill: var(--col-text-2);
    }

    /* Put it up here because following classes have more priority */
    .highlightLastMove {
        background-color: var(--highlight-recent) !important;
    }

    .highlight {
        background-color: var(--highlight-hover) !important;
    }

    .highlightSecondary {
        background-color: var(--highlight-connected) !important;
    }


    .highlightGray {
        background-color: var(--highlight-grayscale) !important;
    }

    .highlightWinning {
        background-color: var(--highlight-win) !important;
    }

    /* Combined highlights */
    .highlightLastMove.highlightSecondary {
        background-color: var(--highlight-recent-connected) !important;
    }

    .highlightLastMove.highlight {
        background-color: var(--highlight-recent-hover) !important;
    }

    @media (max-width: 600px) {
        .game {
            padding: 0 0.5em;
        }

        .board {
            margin-inline: 0.5em;
        }
    }
</style>